after solving these equation, we get
$\begin{aligned}
& x=\frac{-1}{\sqrt{2}}, y=\frac{ \pm 1}{\sqrt{2}} \\
\Rightarrow & \sqrt{-\mathrm{i}}= \pm\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}-\frac{\mathrm{i}}{\sqrt{2}}\right) \pm \frac{1-\mathrm{i}}{\sqrt{2}}=\frac{1-\mathrm{i}}{\sqrt{2}} \text{$ or $} \frac{-1+\mathrm{i}}{\sqrt{2}}
\end{aligned}$

